      "word_count": 21,
      "title": "John Murtagh General Practice",
      "author": "John",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "Page xiv\nMaking the most of your book\nDiagnostic strategy models\nDiagnostic strategy models for common presenting problems form the backbone of this\nbook. General Practice is renowned for this unique and powerful learning feature, which\nwas introduced in the first edition.\nKey facts and checkpoints\nKey facts and checkpoints provide accurate statistics and local and global contexts.\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 29,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "char_count": 385,
      "word_count": 58,
      "title": "John Murtagh General Practice",
      "author": "John",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "Page xv\nThe staff of Asclepius\nThe staff of Asclepius icon highlights diseases for when you are specifically searching\nfor information on a particular disease.\nRed and yellow flags\nRed and yellow flags alert you to potential dangers. Red is the most urgent, but yellow\nalso requires careful consideration.\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 30,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "char_count": 306,
      "word_count": 49,
      "title": "John Murtagh General Practice",
      "author": "John",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "Clinical framework\nClinical framework based on major steps of clinical features, investigations, diagnosis,\nmanagement and treatment reflects the key activities in the daily tasks of general\npractitioners.\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 31,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "char_count": 206,
      "word_count": 27,
      "title": "John Murtagh General Practice",
      "author": "John",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "Page xvi\nSeven masquerades checklist\nThis unique feature of the book reminds you of potential and hidden dangers underlying\npatient presentations.\nDiagnostic triads\nKey features that may discriminate between one disease and another are clearly\npresented.\nEvidence-based research\nEvidence-based research is recognised with a full chapter on research in general\npractice and evidence base, including more on qualitative models. In addition,\nsubstantial references are provided for every chapter.\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 32,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "char_count": 494,
      "word_count": 68,
      "title": "John Murtagh General Practice",
      "author": "John",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "Extensive coverage of paediatric and geriatric care, pregnancy\nand complementary therapies\nExtensive coverage of paediatric and geriatric care, pregnancy and complementary\ntherapies is integrated throughout, as well as devoted chapter content providing more\ncomprehensive information in these areas.\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 33,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "char_count": 300,
      "word_count": 38,
      "title": "John Murtagh General Practice",
      "author": "John",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "Page xvii\nPractice tips\nPractice tips consist of key points that are of use in the clinical setting.\nClinical photos\nClinical photos provide authentic, visual examples of many conditions and serve as\neither a valuable introduction or confirmation of diagnosis.\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 34,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "char_count": 261,
      "word_count": 40,
      "title": "John Murtagh General Practice",
      "author": "John",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "Full colour illustrations\nFull colour illustrations are provided, with more than 600 diagrams in the clean, simple\nstyle that has proved so popular.\nSignificantly enhanced index\nThe index has more sub-categories with bold page numbers indicating the main\ntreatment of a topic, enabling you to quickly pinpoint the most relevant information.\nPage numbers in italics refer to figures and tables. Entries with ‘see also’ have cross-\nreferences to related, but more specific information on the topic.\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 35,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
