    "text": "Page 8\n 1\n 2\n 3\n 4\nFIGURE 1.3  The family life cycle (approximate time in each stage)17, 18\nResources\nThe World Organization of National Colleges, Academies and Academic Associations of\nGeneral Practitioners/Family Physicians (WONCA). Available from:\nwww.globalfamilydoctor.com, accessed February 2021.\nAustralian Government, Institute of Family Studies. Family Matters No. 87, 2011. Think Family:\nA new approach to Families at Risk. Available from:\nhttps://aifs.gov.au/sites/default/files/fm87e.pdf, accessed February 2021.\nReferences\nAmerican Academy of Family Physicians. Official definition of Family Practice and\nFamily Physician (AAFP Publication No. 303). Kansas City, Mo: AAFP, 1986.\nRakel RE. Essentials of Family Practice. Philadelphia: WB Saunders Company, 1993: 2–\n3.\nRACGP. What is General Practice? Available from:\nhttps://www.racgp.org.au/becomingagp/what-is-a-gp/what-is-general-practice/, accessed\nFebruary 2021.\nAnderson NA, Bridges-Webb C, Chancellor AHB. General Practice in Australia. Sydney:\nSydney University Press, 1986: 3–4.\n",
