  {
    "text": "Table 11.9\nReview exercise and physical activity\nReview HbA1c (test at least every 6 months)\nReview lipid levels (test every 12 months)\nDiabetes control: an annual review program4\n1 History\nSmoking and alcohol use\nSymptoms of hypoglycaemia, hyperglycaemia\nCheck symptoms relating to eyes, circulation, feet*\nImmunisation\n2 Examinations\nWeight, height, BMI\nBlood pressure—standing and lying\nExamine heart*\nCarotid and peripheral pulses*\nEyes:\nvisual acuity (Snellen chart)\n?cataracts\noptic fundi (or ophthalmologist referral)*\n?diabetic retinal photography\nTendon reflexes and sensation for peripheral neuropathy*\nSkin (general)\nFoot examination including footwear*\nCheck injection sites\nUrine examination: albumin, ketones, glucose\n3 Review biochemical levels\n*These items comprise a program for detection of long-term complications. They should be conducted annually, commencing 5 years after\ndiagnosis.\nPatient education resources\nHand-out sheets from Murtagh’s Patient Education 8th edition:\nDiabetes\n",
