  },
  {
    "text": "Table 18.1\nThe typical clinical features are presented in TABLE 18.1\n and FIGURE 18.2\n.\nFIGURE 18.2  Clinical features of Epstein–Barr mononucleosis\nClinical features of EBM1,3,4\nSymptoms\nSlow-onset malaise 1–6 weeks\nFever\nMyalgia\nHeadaches, anorexia\nBlocked nose—mouth breathing\nNasal quality to voice\nSore throat (85%)\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 432,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
