    }
  },
  {
    "text": "FIGURE 18.4  Possible clinical features of primary HIV infection\nClinical features of progression—chronic fever, cough <1 month, chronic diarrhoea, oral thrush,\nweight loss.\nFever\nUsually this is of unknown origin\nWeight loss\nUsually severe and muscle wasting\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
