      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "Page 199\nFIGURE 20.3  Opisthotonos caused by advanced meningitis\nChildren over 3 years, adolescents, adults\nMeningeal irritation more obvious (e.g. headache, fever, vomiting, neck stiffness)\nLater: delirium, altered conscious state\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 496,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "char_count": 232,
      "word_count": 30,
      "title": "John Murtagh General Practice",
