      "year": "2020",
      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "FIGURE 25.3  Time course of IgG and IgM antibodies in viral arthritis\nPlain X-ray is invaluable, although in some conditions radiological changes may be apparent\nonly when the disease is well established. Typical X-ray changes for common conditions are\npresented in FIGURE 25.4\n. Arthrography has limited value in the diagnosis of polyarthritis but\nis very useful for specific joints such as the shoulder and the knee. Ultrasound examination for\njoints such as the shoulder and the hip can be very useful.\n",
