  {
    "text": "FIGURE 25.9  Rheumatoid arthritis: typical joint distribution\nClinical features\nInsidious onset but can begin acutely (explosive RA)\nAny age 10–75 years: peak 30–50 years but bimodal 25–50 (peak age) and 65–75\nFemale to male ratio = 3:1\nJoint pain: worse on waking, nocturnal pain, disturbed sleep; relieved with activity\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 704,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
