  {
    "text": "Page 289\nThe various possible extra-articular manifestations are summarised in FIGURE 25.11\n.\nFIGURE 25.11  Rheumatoid arthritis: significant non-articular clinical\nmanifestations\nInvestigations\nESR/CRP usually raised according to activity of disease\nAnaemia (normochromic and normocytic) may be present\nRheumatoid factor\npositive in about 70–80% (less frequent in early disease)\n15–25% of RA patients will remain negative21\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 707,
