    "text": "Table 28.1\nA summary of the diagnostic strategy model is presented in TABLE 28.1\n.\nLow back pain: diagnostic strategy model\nProbability diagnosis\nVertebral dysfunction (non-specific low back pain)\nMusculoligamentous strain/sprain\nSpondylosis (degenerative OA)\nSerious disorders not to be missed\nCardiovascular:\nruptured aortic aneurysm\nretroperitoneal haemorrhage (anticoagulants)\nNeoplasia:\nmyeloma\ncarcinoma of pancreas\nmetastases\nSevere infections:\nvertebral osteomyelitis\nepidural abscess\nseptic discitis\ntuberculosis\npelvic abscess/PID\nOsteoporotic compression fracture/other fracture\nCauda equina compression\nPitfalls (often missed)\nSpondyloarthropathies:\nankylosing spondylitis\nreactive arthritis\npsoriasis\nbowel inflammation\nSacroiliac dysfunction\nSpondylolisthesis\nClaudication:\nvascular\nneurogenic/spinal canal stenosis\nPaget disease\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 789,
