    }
  },
  {
    "text": "Crushing\nVice-like\nBurning\nAching\nTightness\nBurning\nHeavy\nSearing\nPain site\nDeep\nretrosternal\nDeep\nretrosternal\nRetrosternal\nAnterior chest\nPain\nradiation\nThroat/lower\njaw\nLeft arm\n(often)\nRight arm\n(uncommon)\nBack\n(uncommon)\nAs for\ninfarction\nLateral chest\n(pleuritic)\nFront to back o\nchest\nDown back to\nabdomen\nArms\nHistory\nFamily, risk\nfactors\nFamily, risk\nfactors\nPhlebitis\nCalf pain\nImmobility\nSurgery\nMalignancy\nAtherosclerosi\nHypertension\n?Marfan\nAssociated\nsymptoms\nPallor,\nnausea,\nsweating,\nvomiting,\ndyspnoea,\nsyncope\nStrangling in\nthroat\nDyspnoea,\nsyncope,\nsweating,\nvomiting,\ncyanosis,\nagitation,\nhaemoptysis\nSyncope, pallo\ncyanosis,\nNeurological:\nhemipares\nparaplegia\nPulse\nVariable\narrhythmias\nVariable\narrhythmias\nTachycardia\nUnequal, some\nabsent\nCardiac\nauscultation\n± Gallop\nrhythm\nmurmur of MI\nS3 during\nattack\n↓ Pulmonary\nS2, S3 or S4\n± Murmur of Al\nChest\nauscultation\nBasal\ncrackles\n±\nAdventitious\nsounds\nChest X-ray\n± Localised\noligaemia or\ninfarction\nWidening of\nmediastinum\nECG\nQ waves ST\nelevation T\ninversion\nNormal or ST\ndepression\nR axis\ndeviation S1,\nQ3, T3 sign\nMay show\nmyocardial\ninfarction\n",
    "metadata": {
