      "word_count": 161,
      "title": "John Murtagh General Practice",
      "author": "John",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "discharge without pain. The discharge occurs through a perforation in the TM: one is safe (see\nFIG. 39.10A\n), the other unsafe (see FIG. 39.10B\n).\nFIGURE 39.10 (a) Chronic otitis media with loss of the tympanic membrane;\nthis is ‘safe ear’, (b) unsafe ear: chronic otitis media with attic cholesteatoma\n Chronic discharging otitis media (safe)5,15\nIf aural discharge persists for >6 weeks after a course of antibiotics, treatment can be with topical\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 1156,
