  },
  {
    "text": "FIGURE 55.1  Dermatomes of the lower limb, representing approximate\ncutaneous distribution of the nerve roots\nOther important causes of referred thigh pain include ischiogluteal bursitis (weaver’s bottom)\nand gluteus medius tendinitis or trochanteric bursitis.\nSerious disorders not to be missed\nNeoplasia\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 1575,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
