    }
  },
  {
    "text": "FIGURE 56.15  Sites of rupture of the anterior cruciate ligament\nMechanisms\nSudden change in direction with leg in momentum\nInternal tibial rotation on a flexed knee (commonest) (e.g. during pivoting)\nMarked valgus force (e.g. a rugby tackle)\nMay be associated with collateral ligament tears and meniscus injuries. The so-called\n‘unhappy triad’ is a ruptured ACL, medial meniscus tear and medial collateral ligament tear.\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 1638,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
