    }
  },
  {
    "text": "FIGURE 58.2  Paget disease: possible clinical features\nDiagnosis\nRaised serum ALP level (often very high >1000 U/L). A result >125 U/L suggests active\ndisease.6\nNote: Calcium and phosphate normal.\nPlain X-ray: dense expanded bone—best seen in skull and pelvis.\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 1710,
