  {
    "text": "Table 59.4\nFIGURE 59.5  Diagrammatic mechanism of re-entry tachycardia\nElectrophysiological classification of common antiarrhythmic drugs\n(Vaughan Williams)\nClass Drug\nUsual dosage\nCommon side effects\nI\nMembrane\ndepressant drugs\n(sodium-channel\nblockers)\nIa\nDisopyramide\nProcainamide\nQuinidine\n100–200 mg qid\n1 g qid IV use\n2–3 SR tabs\n(0.25 g) bd\nBlurred vision, dry mouth,\nurinary problems in males\n(avoid in men >50)\nAnorexia, nausea, urticaria\nDiarrhoea, headache,\ntinnitus\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
