      "word_count": 213,
      "title": "John Murtagh General Practice",
      "author": "John",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "FIGURE 62.3  Tonsillitis of Epstein–Barr mononucleosis showing swollen red\ntonsils, with a whitish-yellow membranous exudate, swollen uvula and\npetechiae on the soft palate\nPhoto courtesy Hugh Newton-John\nFIGURE 62.4  Acute follicular tonsillitis due to Streptococcus pyogenes: the\ntonsils are red and swollen with pockets of pus\nPhoto courtesy Hugh Newton-John\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 1801,
      "chunk_index": 0,
