  {
    "text": "Table 63.2\nTiredness/chronic fatigue: diagnostic\nstrategy model\nProbability diagnosis\nStress and anxiety\nDepression\nInappropriate lifestyle and psychosocial factors\nViral/postviral infection\nSleep-related disorders (e.g. sleep apnoea)\nSerious disorders not to be missed\nVascular:\ncardiac arrhythmias\ncardiomyopathy\nincipient CCF\nInfection:\nhidden abscess\nHIV/AIDS\nhepatitis B and C\nothers\nCancer, any malignancy\nOther:\nanaemia\nhaemochromatosis\nPitfalls (often missed)\n‘Masked’ depression\nCoeliac disease\nChronic infection (e.g. Lyme disease)\nIncipient CCF\nFibromyalgia\nLack of fitness\nDrugs: alcohol, prescribed, withdrawal\nMenopause syndrome\nPregnancy\nNeurological disorders:\npost head injury\nCVA\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 1818,
      "chunk_index": 0,
