    "text": "the thyroid and signs of hyperthyroidism\nthe abdomen (check liver, any masses and tenderness)\nrectal examination (test stool for occult blood)\nreflexes\nlook for acid dental erosion on surface of upper teeth (bulimia)\nInvestigations\nBasic investigations include:\nhaemoglobin, red cell indices and film\nwhite cell count\nESR/CRP\nthyroid function test\nrandom blood sugar\nEUC, LFTs\nchest X-ray\nurine analysis\nfaecal occult blood\nOthers to consider:\nupper GIT (endoscopy or barium meal)\nHIV serology\nultrasound of abdomen (or CT if suspected abnormality not found)\ncolonoscopy\ntumour markers, e.g. CA-125, CEA\nWeight loss in children\nWeight loss in children can be considered as:\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 1927,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
