  },
  {
    "text": "FIGURE 76.1  A stepwise pharmacological management approach to systolic\nheart failure12,14\nNew agents9\nIvabradine is a direct sinus node inhibitor which can be added to a beta blocker in patients with\ncontinuing symptoms of moderate to severe failure, or where beta blockers are contraindicated or\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 2113,
