    "text": " 4\n 5\n 6\n 7\n 8\n 9\n10\nKumar PJ, Clark M. Clinical Medicine (7th edn). London: Elsevier Saunders, 2009: 625–\n42.\nRACGP. Royal Australian College of General Practitioners Guidelines for Preventive\nActivities in General Practice (9th edn). East Melbourne: RACGP, 2016: 96–7.\nTally N, O’Connor S. Clinical Examinations (5th edn). Sydney: Maclennan & Petty, 2006:\n186–7.\nRobinson MJ, Roberton DM. Practical Paediatrics (5th edn). Melbourne: Churchill\nLivingstone, 2003: 610–1.\nCunninghan M. Drug therapy in the renally challenged. Monash University Update for\nGPs. Seminar proceedings November, 2005: 1–8.\nThomas MC. Diuretics, ACE inhibitors and NSAIDs—‘the triple whammy’. Med J Aust,\n21 Feb 2000: 172.\nAhmed A, Jorna T, Bhandari S. Should we STOP angiotensin converting enzyme\ninhibitors/angiotensin receptor blockers in advanced kidney disease? Nephron, 2016; 133:\n147–58.\n",
