    "text": "prone\nGrasps objects handed\nto him or her\nemerging (possibly)\n6 months\nPropped-up sitting\n(independent sitting 7–8\nmonths)\nHands down in front of\nhim or her, hands to\nfeet\nKeeping head level with\nbody when pulled to a\nsitting position\nRolling-up on extended\narm when placed in\nprone and creeping\nwhen placed in prone\nPossibly bangs objects\non a surface\nBabbling well\nestablished\nQuietens and attends\nwhen spoken to\n(listening)\n‘Vocal play’—\nexperimenting with\nnew sounds (e.g.\nblowing raspberries)\nEnjoys interactive\ngames\nSmiles when sees\nparent\nLaughs/squeals with\ndelight\nFriendly to people\n12 months\nTakes weight on feet\nwhen feet plonked on\nground in standing\nposition (parachutes\nthem) or standing\nholding onto furniture\nTransitions by moving in\nand out of positions\nCruising (probably) and\ncrawling\nPoints and follows a\npoint (possibly)\nGrasps with index and\nthumb\nClaps hands\nWaves goodbye\nLots of conversational\nbabble\nA couple of words\n(‘Mum’, ‘Dad’, other)\nprobably\nPossible separation\nand/or stranger anxiety\nLooks for objects out\nof direct line of vision\n(dropped toy)\nCo-looking at pictures\nin books or objects\n(shared attention)\nPossible pointing or\nfollowing a point (‘look\nat the ...’)\nWaves bye-bye\n18 months\nWalks well and probably\nholding hand upstairs\nClimbs on and off\neverything\nFollows 1-step\ncommands (when he\nor she wants to)\nDoes pretend play—\n",
