      "word_count": 193,
      "title": "John Murtagh General Practice",
      "author": "John",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "FIGURE 84.4  Breast hyperplasia in a 15-week-old child\n Growing pains8,9\nGrowing pains (benign nocturnal limb pains) are real and common (around 1 in 5 children).\nFeatures\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 2265,
      "type": "drug_info",
      "char_count": 172,
      "word_count": 26,
      "title": "John Murtagh General Practice",
      "author": "John",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "Typical age 3–12 years\nPositive family history\nUsually bilateral and non-articular\nPoorly localised in leg—typical sites include shins, calves, thighs, popliteal fossa (see\nFIG. 84.5\n)\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 2266,
