      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "FIGURE 85.10  The tiptoe test for flat feet\n Curly toes\nUsually the third toe curls inward under the second toe so that the second toe lies above the level\nof the first and third toes. The toes can usually be straightened if necessary, so ignore the\nproblem until 2 years. Refer if necessary to have a severe deformity corrected by flexor\ntenotomy.\nA summary of optimal times for surgical intervention in children’s surgical disorders is\npresented in TABLE 85.2\n.\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 2309,
