      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "FIGURE 86.3  Measles showing the typical blotchy, bright red maculopapular\nrash on the face of a miserable child with the three Cs (cough, coryza and\nconjunctivitis)\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 2324,
