      "year": "2020",
      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "FIGURE 86.6  Viral exanthema (fourth syndrome). This mild rubella-like\nmaculopapular rash, which may be caused by a number of viruses, is usually\nnon-pruritic.\n Parvovirus B19 (erythema infectiosum, fifth disease)\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 2330,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "char_count": 214,
      "word_count": 29,
      "title": "John Murtagh General Practice",
      "author": "John",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "Parvovirus, also known as ‘slapped cheek’ syndrome, is a childhood exanthem caused by\nparvovirus strain B19. It occurs typically in young school-aged children. The incubation period\nis 4–20 days. Non-specific prodromal symptoms (fever, runny nose, headache, nausea) are\nfollowed 2–5 days later by the rash. The bright macular rash erupts on the face first (see\nFIG. 86.7\n) then, after a day or so, a maculopapular rash appears on the limbs.1 The rash lasts\nfor only a few days but may recur for several weeks. By the time the rash appears the individual\nusually is no longer infective.\nFIGURE 86.7  Parvovirus, showing the typical slapped cheek appearance\nClinical features\nMild fever (30%) and malaise\nRunny nose, headache, nausea\nPossible lymphadenopathy (especially cervical)\nThe rash (see FIG. 86.8\n):\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 2331,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "char_count": 806,
      "word_count": 128,
      "title": "John Murtagh General Practice",
      "author": "John",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "ssible\n\niphadenopathy erythematous ‘slapped’ cheek\n\nappearance in well child\n\nerythematous\nrash, mainly\non forearms\nand thighs\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 2332,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
