      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "FIGURE 93.3  Changing frequencies of different discrete breast lumps with\nage\nSource: Dixon JM, Mansel RE. Congenital problems and aberrations of normal breast development. In: Dixon JM, ed., ABC of\nBreast Diseases. London: British Medical Journal Publishing Group, 1995. Courtesy of Anthea Carter. Reproduced with permission\nfrom Anthea Carter.\nThe triple test\n1. History and clinical breast examination\n2. Imaging—mammography and/or ultrasound ± MRI\n3. Fine-needle aspiration cytology and/or core biopsy\nThe clinical approach\nThis is based on following a careful history and examination.\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 2505,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "char_count": 590,
