    }
  },
  {
    "text": "Page 1071\nintraduct carcinoma (serous)\nbreast abscess (pus)\nMilky white (galactorrhoea):\nlactation cysts\nlactation\nhyperprolactinaemia\ndrugs (e.g. antipsychotic, cocaine)\nFIGURE 93.5  Woman with advanced breast cancer showing peau d’orange\nsign, brawny oedema and breast retraction\nPeriareolar inflammation\nThis presents as pain around the areola with reddening of the skin, tenderness and\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 2509,
