    "text": "Table 104.3\nFIGURE 104.6  Basic comparison of scrotal lumps\nFeatures of scrotal lumps\nPossible clinical\nsetting\nPosition\nPalpation\nTransillumination\nHydrocele\nAny age\nPrimary or\nsecondary:\ntumour\ninfection\ntorsion\nConfined\nto\nscrotum\nAnterior:\nsurrounds\ntestis\nexcept\nposteriorly\nSmooth,\npear-\nshaped\nLax or\ntense\nTestis\nimpalpable,\nnon-tender\nYes\nCyst of\nepididymis\nAsymptomatic\nor dragging\nBehind and\nabove\nSmooth\nand tense\nYes\n",
