      "char_count": 1251,
      "word_count": 189,
      "title": "John Murtagh General Practice",
      "author": "John",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "FIGURE 106.2  A visual scale of urinary flow. The numbers signify the flow\nrate in millilitres per second. When assessing a patient with voiding\ndysfunction, ask him to indicate which stream is closest to his own.\nComplications of prostatic obstruction\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 2760,
