    "text": " 1\n 2\n 3\n 4\n 5\n 6\n 7\nHypothalmic–pituitary–adrenal axis disruption\nReferences\nMarks R. A diagnosis in dermatology. Aust Fam Physician, 2001; 30(11): 1028–32.\nUsatine RP et al. Color Atlas and Synopsis of Family Medicine (3rd edn). New York:\nMcGraw-Hill Education, 2019: 481.\nMarks R, Sinclair R. A Guide to the Performance of Diagnostic Procedures used in the\nManagement of Common Skin Diseases. Melbourne: Skin & Cancer Foundation\nPublication, 2002: 25–6.\nOverview of diagnosis and management of dermatitis in dermatology [published 2015]. In:\nTherapeutic Guidelines [digital]. Melbourne: Therapeutic Guidelines Limited; 2015.\nwww.tg.org.au, accessed September 2020.\nGambrill J. How much cream? Aust Fam Physician, 1982; 11: 350.\nGeorge CF et al. London: British National Formulary, Number 31, 1996: 451–6.\nUsatine RP et al. Color Atlas and Synopsis of Family Medicine (3rd edn). New York:\nMcGraw-Hill Education, 2019: 681.\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 2883,
