    "text": "FIGURE 115.6  Neurotic excoriations (neurodermatitis) seen on three of four\nextremities. The fourth extremity is a prosthetic leg.17\nPractice tips\nPrinciples of treatment:10\nOccluded and moist wounds heal faster.\nMaintain moist wound environment.\nControl exudate and debris (remove excess—leave enough to allow cellular\nregeneration).\n",
