    }
  },
  {
    "text": "FIGURE 119.1  Normal anatomy of the nail. Diagram of the nail apparatus: (a)\nlateral section view, (b) dorsal surface view\nThe nail bed closely approximates the distal phalanx. The nail has an important functional and\ncosmetic role. It enhances fine touch and motor skills for picking up fine objects, such as a pin\nfrom a flat surface, not possible without fingernails.\nNail disorders and their causes1\nLifting of the nail plate (onycholysis)\nSee FIGURE 119.2\n.\nFIGURE 119.2  Lifting of the nail plate (onycholysis)\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 3126,
