    }
  },
  {
    "text": " 3\n 4\n 5\n 6\n 7\n 8\n 9\n10\nPage 1338\nGrinzi P. Hair and nails. Aust Fam Physician, 2011; 40(7): 471–84.\nByrne M, Howard A. Common nail disorders: how to treat. Australian Doctor, 31 October\n2005: 38–40.\nSinclair R. Treating common nail problems. Aust Fam Physician, 1997; 26: 949–52.\nOnycholysis [published 2015]. In: Therapeutic Guidelines [digital]. Melbourne:\nTherapeutic Guidelines Limited; 2015. www.tg.org.au, accessed April 2021.\nOnychomycosis (tinea of the nails) [published 2015 Nov]. In: Therapeutic Guidelines\n[digital]. Melbourne: Therapeutic Guidelines Limited; 2015. https://www.tg.org.au,\naccessed April 2021.\nThai K. Nail disease: is it fungal and how should it be managed? Medicine Today, 2014;\n15(6): 35–47.\nCrawford F et al. Topical treatments for fungal infections of the skin and nails of the foot.\nCochrane Database Syst Rev, 2000; (2): CD001434.\nMurtagh J, Coleman J. Practice Tips (8th edn). Sydney: McGraw-Hill, 2019.\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "John Murtagh General Practice, 8th Edition.pdf",
      "page": 3149,
      "type": "drug_info",
      "char_count": 940,
      "word_count": 139,
      "title": "John Murtagh General Practice",
      "author": "John",
      "year": "2020",
