      "year": "2020",
      "edition": "8th"
    }
  },
  {
    "text": " 1\nPage 1477\nSlow extraction of pre-emerging worms as they exit the skin\nMetronidazole ± corticosteroids\nPatient education resources\nHand-out sheets from Murtagh’s Patient Education 8th edition:\nBacterial meningitis and meningococcus\nDengue fever\nMalaria\nRabies\nTravel: air travel\nTravel: guide for travellers\nTravel sickness\nTuberculosis\nWest Nile virus\nWorms\nZika virus\nResources\nWorld Health Organization, International travel and health: www.who.int/ith/en\nTravel Doctor-TMVC: www.traveldoctor.com.au\nSmartraveller (country-specific information provided by the Australian Government):\nhttp://smartraveller.gov.au\nCenters for Disease Control and Prevention: www.cdc.gov/travel\nReferences\nLocke DM. Traveller’s diarrhoea. Aust Fam Physician, 1990; 19: 194–203.\n",
