      "year": "2020",
      "edition": ""
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "94\nDeafness\n■\n■\nImpedance tympanometry\nIncreased impedance (reduced compliance) with otitis media \nwith effusion.\n■\n■\nMRI\nAcoustic neuroma, brain tumour.\n!\n• Progressive unilateral deafness accompanied by \ntinnitus, vertigo or neurological symptoms or signs \nshould prompt urgent investigation for an acoustic \nneuroma.\nSUBASH KC/NMC-15TH/2014\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "Churchills_Pocketbook_of_Differential_Diagnosis (1).pdf",
      "page": 107,
