  {
    "text": "B978-0-7020-3222-6.00021-3, 00021\nB978-0-7020-3222-6.00021-3, 00021\n104\nDIZZINESS\nSPECIFIC INVESTIGATIONS\n■\n■\n24-hour ECG\nTo screen for arrhythmia.\n■\n■\nAudiometry\nAllows assessment and classification of any accompanying \nhearing loss.\n■\n■\nCarotid Doppler\nTo evaluate patency of the vessel and to screen for the presence \nof plaque (TIAs).\n■\n■\nECHO\nTo evaluate aortic valve.\n■\n■\nCT head\nStroke, cerebellar haemorrhage, evaluation of severe head \ninjuries.\n■\n■\nMRI\nAcoustic neuroma and other cerebellopontine angle tumours, \ndemyelination with multiple sclerosis.\n■\n■\nEEG\nTo detect seizure activity.\n!\n• Dizziness accompanied by other symptoms such as \nloss of consciousness, palpitations or neurological \nsymptoms should be investigated immediately.\n• Dizziness associated with an aortic murmur requires \nurgent referral. Significant aortic stenosis is a cause \nof sudden death.\nSUBASH KC/NMC-15TH/2014\n",
