    "text": "B978-0-7020-3222-6.00025-0, 00025\nB978-0-7020-3222-6.00025-0, 00025\n119\nEYE DISORDERS\nMost eye disorders tend to present as the ‘red eye’. It is the single \nmost common ophthalmic complaint encountered by general \npractitioners.\nCAUSES\nEYELIDS\n• Stye (hordeolum)\n• Xanthelasma\n• Blepharitis\n• Meibomian cyst\n• Entropion\n• Ectropion\nEYE\nSURFACE\n• Trauma\n• Foreign body\nCONJUNCTIVA\n• Conjunctivitis\n• Bacterial\n• Viral\n• Allergic\n• Chlamydial\n• Subconjunctival haemorrhage\nSCLERA\n• Episcleritis\n• Scleritis\nCORNEA\n• Corneal abrasion\n• Corneal ulceration (keratitis)\n• Viral\n• Bacterial\n• Fungal\nIRIS AND CILIARY BODY\n• Iridocyclitis (uveitis)\nINTRAOCULAR\n• Acute angle-closure glaucoma\nSection A\nSUBASH KC/NMC-15TH/2014\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "Churchills_Pocketbook_of_Differential_Diagnosis (1).pdf",
      "page": 132,
      "type": "list",
      "char_count": 718,
      "word_count": 101,
      "title": "Churchills Pocketbook Of Differential Diagnosis (1)",
      "author": "Unknown Author",
      "year": "2020",
