    "text": "B978-0-7020-3222-6.00033-X, 00033\nB978-0-7020-3222-6.00033-X, 00033\n156\nFoot Pain\n!\n• Sudden onset of pain in the foot in an arteriopathy \nor in a patient with atrial fibrillation is likely to be \ndue to ischaemia. Examine the pulses. Urgent \nreferral is usually required.\n• Systemic illness and fever with localised severe bone \npain may suggest osteomyelitis or septic arthritis. \nRisk factors include diabetes and immunosuppression. \nUrgent investigation is required.\n• Pain with no obvious signs, especially lack of \nlocalised tenderness, may suggest neuropathy or \nan L5/S1 nerve lesion.\nSUBASH KC/NMC-15TH/2014\n",
