      "year": "2020",
      "edition": ""
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "201\nSection A\nHallucinations\n!\n• Hallucinations in children with febrile illness are \ncommon.\n• Pure olfactory hallucinations are strongly suggestive \nof temporal lobe epilepsy.\n• Tactile hallucinations strongly suggest acute alcohol \nwithdrawal.\nSUBASH KC/NMC-15TH/2014\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "Churchills_Pocketbook_of_Differential_Diagnosis (1).pdf",
      "page": 214,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "char_count": 271,
