  {
    "text": "249\nJAW PAIN AND SWELLINGS\nSection A\nSPECIAL INVESTIGATIONS\n■\n■\nBlood cultures\nOsteomyelitis.\n■\n■\nECG\nMyocardial ischaemia.\n■\n■\nEBV serology\nBurkitt’s lymphoma.\n■\n■\nBiopsy\nBenign versus malignant lesions.\n!\n• Painless, progressive swelling of the jaw suggests \ntumour or dental cyst and requires urgent dental \nreferral.\nSUBASH KC/NMC-15TH/2014\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "Churchills_Pocketbook_of_Differential_Diagnosis (1).pdf",
      "page": 262,
      "chunk_index": 0,
