    }
  },
  {
    "text": "294\nLEG SWELLINGS\n!\n• Patients with unexplained DVT may have underlying \nmalignancy. Take a full systematic history.\n• In the young patient with unilateral oedema \nof slow onset, always consider lymphoedema. \nLymphoedema does not pit.\nSUBASH KC/NMC-15TH/2014\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "Churchills_Pocketbook_of_Differential_Diagnosis (1).pdf",
      "page": 307,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
