    }
  },
  {
    "text": "B978-0-7020-3222-6.00075-4, 00075\nB978-0-7020-3222-6.00075-4, 00075\n362\nPOLYURIA\n!\n• Polyuria accompanied by polydipsia is often the first \npresentation of both type 1 and type 2 diabetes \nmellitus. Urgent investigation is required.\n• Diabetes mellitus is not the only cause of polyuria \naccompanied by thirst. If urinalysis is negative for \nsugar, diabetes insipidus or hypercalcaemia are \npossible diagnoses.\nSUBASH KC/NMC-15TH/2014\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "Churchills_Pocketbook_of_Differential_Diagnosis (1).pdf",
