  {
    "text": "383\nRASHES\nSection A\nErythema\nInfection\n• Cellulitis, e.g. streptococcal\n• Viral, e.g. measles\n• HIV\nTraumatic\n• Burns (thermal, chemical, sunburn)\nDrugs\n• Antibiotics\n• NSAIDs\nSystemic disease\n• Chronic liver disease (palmar erythema)\n• SLE (butterfly rash)\nOther\n• Gout\n• Rosacea\n• Erythema ab igne\n• ‘Deck chair legs’\nSPECIFIC ERYTHEMATOUS CONDITIONS\nErythema multiforme (‘target’ lesions)\nSevere form is known as Stevens–Johnson syndrome\nInfection\n• Herpes simplex virus\n• Mycoplasma\n• O\u0007rf\nCollagen disorders\nDrugs\n• Barbiturates\n• Sulphonamides\n• Penicillin\nErythema nodosum (raised, red, painful lesions \ncommonly on shins)\nInfection\n• TB\n• (commoner where TB is endemic)\nSUBASH KC/NMC-15TH/2014\n",
