  {
    "text": "B978-0-7020-3222-6.00083-3, 00083\nB978-0-7020-3222-6.00083-3, 00083\n400\nscrotal pain\n■\n■\nMRI\nSpinal lesion.\n■\n■\nSurgery\nDiagnostic between torsion and infection. There is rarely time or \nequipment to carry out laser Doppler or a technetium scan. If a \ntesticular torsion is not dealt with within 6 hours of onset there \nis likely to be permanent damage to the testis. If there is any \ndoubt in the diagnosis, assume that it is torsion and explore the \nscrotum surgically.\n!\n• It is difficult, if not impossible, to distinguish \nbetween torsion and epididymo-orchitis. Urgent \nreferral and surgical exploration is required.\nSUBASH KC/NMC-15TH/2014\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "Churchills_Pocketbook_of_Differential_Diagnosis (1).pdf",
      "page": 413,
      "chunk_index": 0,
