    }
  },
  {
    "text": "415\nSplenomegaly\nSection A\n■\n■\nELISA/immunofluorescence\nTyphus.\n■\n■\nBone marrow aspirate\nMyelofibrosis. Polycythaemia. Leukaemia. Gaucher’s disease.\n■\n■\nUS\nCause of splenomegaly, e.g. cyst, tumour, diffuse enlargement. \nCirrhosis of the liver.\n■\n■\nCT\nCauses of splenomegaly, e.g. cyst, tumour, diffuse enlargement, \ncirrhosis.\n!\n• The spleen may enlarge massively. Palpation for \nsuspected splenomegaly should begin in the right \nlower quadrant.\nSUBASH KC/NMC-15TH/2014\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "Churchills_Pocketbook_of_Differential_Diagnosis (1).pdf",
