    "text": "419\nSteatorrhoea\nSection A\n!\n• Always take a careful history as the patient may \nactually complain of diarrhoea. In steatorrhoea \nthe stool is classically described as pale, fatty and \noffensive and difficult to flush away. Clear distinction \nbetween diarrhoea and steatorrhoea is important.\nSUBASH KC/NMC-15TH/2014\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "Churchills_Pocketbook_of_Differential_Diagnosis (1).pdf",
      "page": 432,
      "chunk_index": 0,
