      "year": "2020",
      "edition": ""
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "510\nHypocalcaemia\n■\n■\nSerum amylase\nCa  associated with acute pancreatitis.\n■\n■\nSerum magnesium\n Mg – magnesium deficiency may lead to hypocalcaemia.\n■\n■\nPTH levels\nHypoparathyroidism.\n■\n■\nSerum Vitamin D\nvitamin D deficiency.\n■\n■\nECG\nProlonged QT interval. Prolonged ST interval.\n!\n• The first symptom of hypocalcaemia is circumoral \nparaesthesia. If this occurs after thyroid or \nparathyroid surgery, it is an indication for an \nurgent check of the serum calcium and appropriate \ntreatment.\nSUBASH KC/NMC-15TH/2014\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "Churchills_Pocketbook_of_Differential_Diagnosis (1).pdf",
      "page": 523,
