    "text": "120\n120\nChapter 3  Medicine\nPitfalls in CXR analysis for possible pneumothorax\n\t•\t When using digital images, always use a picture archiving and communication \nsystem (PACS) workstation. The signs of pneumothorax may be subtle and \ndifﬁcult to spot. Compare with previous CXRs, if available.\n\t•\t Look for a displacement of the pleural line.\n\t•\t Do not mistake the scapular edge for the lung edge. Similarly, clothing, \nO2 tubing, and overlying sheets can cause artefacts which mimic the \nedge of the lung.\n\t•\t Some patients with COPD have emphysematous bullae, which can \nmimic pneumothorax. If in doubt, ask for senior review prior to treating \nfor pneumothorax.\n\t•\t An air–​ﬂuid level at the costophrenic angle may be present.\nFig. 3.28  CXR showing spontaneous right pneumothorax.\n \n",
