    "text": "  \n187\nToxicology\nPoisons: background  188\nDiagnosis of poisoning  190\nPoisons: supportive care  191\nReducing absorption of poison  192\nAntidotes for poisons  194\nOpioid poisoning  196\nSalicylate poisoning  197\nParacetamol poisoning  198\nManagement of paracetamol poisoning  200\nTricyclic antidepressant poisoning  202\nBenzodiazepine poisoning  204\nClomethiazole poisoning  204\nPhenothiazine poisoning  204\nBarbiturate poisoning  205\nLithium poisoning  205\nSulfonylurea poisoning  205\nBeta-​blocker poisoning  206\nCalcium antagonist poisoning  206\nDigoxin poisoning  207\nACE inhibitor poisoning  207\nTheophylline poisoning  208\nSalbutamol poisoning  208\nIron poisoning  209\nEthanol poisoning  210\nMethanol poisoning  211\nEthylene glycol poisoning  212\nParaquat poisoning  213\nPetrol and parafﬁn poisoning  213\nOrganophosphate poisoning  214\nCyanide poisoning  215\nCarbon monoxide poisoning  216\nChlorine poisoning  217\nCS gas (tear gas)  217\nChemical incidents  218\nPlants, berries, and mushrooms  219\nButton batteries  220\nNovel psychoactive substances  221\nRecreational drugs  222\nSerotonin syndrome  224\nBody packers  225\nChapter 4\n \n",
