    "text": "  \n281\nAnalgesia and anaesthesia\nApproach to pain  282\nOptions for relieving pain  283\nAnalgesics: aspirin and paracetamol  284\nAnalgesics: NSAIDs  285\nAnalgesics: morphine  286\nAnalgesics: Entonox® and ketamine  287\nAnalgesics: other opioids  288\nPenthrox®  286\nAnalgesia for trauma  289\nAnalgesia in speciﬁc situations  290\nLocal anaesthesia  292\nLocal anaesthetic toxicity  294\nAdrenaline (epinephrine) in LA  295\nGeneral principles of local anaesthesia  296\nTopical anaesthesia  298\nLocal anaesthetic administration  299\nBier’s block  300\nLocal anaesthetic nerve blocks  302\nIntercostal nerve block  303\nDigital nerve block  304\nMedian and ulnar nerve blocks  306\nRadial nerve block at the wrist  308\nDental anaesthesia  309\nNerve blocks of forehead and ear  310\nFascia iliaca compartment block  312\nFemoral nerve block  313\nNerve blocks at the ankle  314\nApproach to sedation  316\nDrugs for IV sedation  318\nSedation in children  319\nGeneral anaesthesia in the ED  320\nEmergency anaesthesia and rapid sequence induction  322\nDifﬁcult intubation  324\nGeneral anaesthetic drugs  326\nChapter 7\n \n",
