    "text": "  \nBurns: assessment\n399\nA\nB\nC\n1\n2\n13\nC\nB\n2\n1\nA\n1\n2\n13\n2\nB\nB\nC\nC\n21/2\n21/2\n11/2\n11/2\n11/2\n11/2\n11/2\n11/2\n11/2\n11/2\n13/4\n13/4\n13/4\n13/4\nFig. 8.25  Assessing extent of burns—​Lund and Browder charts.\nTable 8.5  Relative percentage of area affected by growth (age in years)\n \n0\n1\n5\n10\n15\nAdult\nA: half of head\n91/​2\n81/​2\n61/​2\n51/​2\n41/​2\n31/​2\nB: half of thigh\n23/​4\n31/​4\n4\n41/​2\n41/​2\n43/​4\nC: half of leg\n21/​2\n21/​2\n23/​4\n3\n31/​4\n31/​2\nAdults—​rule of 9s:\nHead\n= 9%\nEach arm\n= 9%\nEach leg\n= 18%\nFront of trunk\n= 18%\nBack of trunk\n= 18%\nPerineum\n= 1%\nInfants—​rule of 5s:\nHead\n= 20%\nEach arm\n= 10%\nEach leg\n= 20%\nFront of trunk\n= 10%\nBack of trunk\n= 10%\n",
