    "text": "408\n408\nChapter 9\nWounds, fractures, and \northopaedics\nThe approach to wounds  410\nForensic classification of wounds  411\nFurther assessment of skin wounds  412\nPuncture wounds and foreign bodies  413\nWound cleaning and prophylactic antibiotics  414\nWound closure  415\nSutures  416\nWound aftercare  418\nInfected wounds and cellulitis  419\nBite wounds  420\nSpeciﬁc bites and stings  422\nTetanus prophylaxis  424\nNeedlestick injury  425\nHow to describe a fracture  426\nOpen (compound) fractures  428\nDislocations (and subluxations)  429\nCasts and their problems  430\nFractures and osteoporosis  431\nSoft tissue injuries  432\nOther soft tissue problems  433\nPhysiotherapy in the ED  434\nFracture clinic and alternatives  436\nApproach to hand injuries  438\nClinical signs of hand injury  440\nHand wounds and associated injuries  442\nHand fractures and dislocations  444\nThumb fractures and dislocations  446\nSoft tissue hand injuries  448\nOther soft tissue hand problems  449\nScaphoid fracture  450\nLunate dislocation  452\nOther carpal injuries  453\nColles’ fracture  454\nManipulating Colles’ fractures  456\nSmith’s fracture  457\nBarton’s and reverse Barton’s fracture  458\nSoft tissue wrist injuries/​problems  459\nForearm fractures and related injury  460\nElbow injuries  462\nDislocated elbow  464\n \n",
