    "text": "  \n647\nAcute bronchiolitis  698\nWhooping coughND  700\nPulmonary tuberculosisND  701\nCystic ﬁbrosis  701\nPneumonia  702\nFits in children  704\nStatus epilepticus  705\nFebrile convulsions  706\nFunny turns  707\nDiabetic ketoacidosis  708\nUrinary tract infection  710\nHaematuria  712\nAcute kidney injury  714\nPoisoning in children  716\nPrevention of paediatric poisoning  717\nGastroenteritis in children  718\nAbdominal pain in children  720\nInguinal and scrotal swellings  722\nForeskin problems and zip entrapment  724\nThe limping child  726\nThe painful hip  728\nOsteochondritis  730\nMajor paediatric trauma  732\nInjury prevention  733\nResuscitation of the injured child  734\nAssessing head injuries in children  736\nManaging head injuries in children  738\nSpinal injury in children  739\nConsiderations in paediatric trauma  740\nWounds in children  741\nPaediatric fractures and dislocations  742\nApproach to limb injuries in children  744\nNormal X-rays in children  746\nShoulder and humeral shaft fractures  747\nSupracondylar humeral fracture  748\nElbow injuries in children  750\nForearm and wrist injuries  751\nHip and femoral fractures in children  752\nPaediatric knee injuries  753\nTibial fractures in children  754\nAnkle and foot injuries in children  755\nChild abuse  756\nPresentation of child abuse: bruising  758\nChild abuse: fractures  759\nChild abuse: head injuries, wounds and burns  760\nNeglect  761\nEmotional abuse  761\nSexual abuse  761\nManagement of child abuse  762\n",
