    "text": "  \nHaematuria\n713\nGlomerulonephritis\nGlomerulonephritis in children is often an immune reaction following an \nURTI due to β-​haemolytic streptococcal infection 2–​3 weeks previously. It \nmay present with haematuria, oliguria ± hypertension and uraemia. Refer \nfor admission and further investigation.\nA similar presentation can occur with Henoch–​Schönlein purpura \n(see % Purpuric rashes, p. 681), SLE, or Berger’s disease (mesangial IgA \nnephropathy).\n \n",
