    "text": "  \nApproach to limb injuries in children\n745\nTable 15.14  Ossiﬁcation centres\nCentre\nFirst appears\nFuses\nHumeral head\n0–​6 months\n18–​21y\nCapitulum\n3–​6 months\n14–​16y\nMedial epicondyle\n4–​7y\n18–​21y\nLateral epicondyle\n9–​13y\n14–​16y\nTrochlea\n9–​10y\n14–​16y\nRadial head\n4–​5y\n14–​17y\nDistal radius\n6–​12 months\n17–​19y\nOlecranon\n9–​11y\n13–​16y\nDistal ulna\n4–​5y\n16–​18y\nCapitate\nBirth to 3 months\n–​\nHamate\nBirth to 4 months\n–​\nTriquetral\n1–​3y\n–​\nLunate\n2–​4y\n–​\nTrapezium\n2–​4y\n–​\nTrapezoid\n3–​5y\n–​\nScaphoid\n3–​5y\n–​\nPisiform\n9–​12y\n–​\nFirst MC base\n1–​3y\n14–​17y\nFemoral head\nBirth to 6 months\n15–​19y\nGreater trochanter\n3–​4y\n17–​19y\nLesser trochanter\n11–​14y\n15–​18y\nDistal femur\nBirth\n17–​20y\nPatella\n2–​6y\n4–​8y\nProximal tibia\nBirth\n15–​18y\nDistal tibia\nBirth to 6 months\n14–​17y\nProximal ﬁbula\n2–​4y\n16–​19y\nDistal ﬁbula\nBirth to 1y\n14–​17y\nPosterior calcaneum\n5–​8y\n13–​16y\nCentral calcaneum\nBirth\n13–​16y\nTalus\nBirth\n–​\nNavicular\n2–​3y\n–​\nCuneiform bones\n1–​3y\n–​\nThese dates are subject to individual variation. In general, epiphyses in girls fuse before those \nin boys.\n",
