    "text": "746\n746\nChapter 15  Paediatric emergencies\nNormal X-​rays in children\nIt is useful to have an idea of the normal appearance of X-​rays in children. \nSome examples are shown in Figs. 15.27–​15.30.\n(a)\n(b)\nFig. 15.27  (a), (b) Normal elbow in a 10y old.\nFig. 15.30  Normal foot in a 2y old.\nFig. 15.29  Normal ankle X-​rays in \na 10y old.\nFig. 15.28  Normal pelvis X-​ray in \na 6y ​old boy.\n \n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "OXFORD HANDBOOK OF EMERGENCY MEDICINE 5TH EDITION (2020).pdf",
