    "text": "Page 39 of 45\n\n®@ The PVCs occur so early that they fall on the T wave of the preceding beat.\n\n®@ These PVCs occur during the refractory period of the ventricles, a vulnerable period because the cardiac\ncells have not fully repolarized.\n\n= ee eee teeee\n\neh teers teers\n\n8 beens tees\n\noe cere\n\n_ eeene\n~\n\nsee\n\nween\nsees neeas\nFears eeees\nseeeieesas\nnewer reese\n\noosee\n\ntie’ ine\neebeew.s\neenkees |\nestes.\n\nRate: Depends on rate of underlying rhythm\nRhythm: Irregular whenever a PVC occurs\n\nP Waves: None associated with the PVC\n\nPR Interval: None associated with the PVC\nQRS: Wide (>0.10 sec), bizarre appearance\n\n",
