lysis removing any very long study: GLP-1 receptor agonists versus placebo,\nOutcome 16: Acute kidney injury (Hazard ratio).................................................................................................................................\n233\nAnalysis 10.1. Comparison 10: Sensitivity analysis removing any very large study: GLP-1 receptor agonists versus placebo,\nOutcome 1: All-cause death.................................................................................................................................................................\n236\nAnalysis 10.2. Comparison 10: Sensitivity analysis removing any very large study: GLP-1 receptor agonists versus placebo,\nOutcome 2: All-cause death (Hazard ratio).........................................................................................................................................\n237\nAnalysis 10.3. Comparison 10: Sensitivity analysis removing any very large study: GLP-1 receptor agonists versus placebo,\nOutcome 3: Cardiovascular death.......................................................................................................................................................\n238\nAnalysis 10.4. Comparison 10: Sensitivity analysis removing any very large study: GLP-1 receptor agonists versus placebo,\nOutcome 4: Cardiovascular death (Hazard ratio)...............................................................................................................................\n239\nAnalysis 10.5. Comparison 10: Sensitivity analysis removing any very large study: GLP-1 receptor agonists versus placebo,\nOutcome 5: 3-point MACE....................................................................................................................................................................\n239\nAnalysis 10.6. Comparison 10: Sensitivity analysis removing any very large study: GLP-1 receptor agonists versus placebo,\nOutcome 6: 3-point MACE (Hazard ratio).......................