    "text": "B, Botros FT, et al. Body weight and eGFR during dulaglutide treatment in type 2 diabetes and moderate-to- severe chronic kidney disease (AWARD-7). Diabetes, Obesity & Metabolism 2019;21(6):1493-7. [PMID: 30762290] Tuttle KR, Rayner B, Lakshmanan M, Woodward B, Kwan A, Konig M, et al. Clinical events in type 2 diabetes and moderate- to-severe CKD by albuminuria status: dulaglutide vs. insulin glargine [abstract no: SA-OR081]. Journal of the American Society of Nephrology 2019;30:102. [EMBASE: 633767837] Tuttle KR, Rayner B, Lakshmanan MC, Kwan AY, Konig M, Shurzinske L, et al. Clinical outcomes by albuminuria status with dulaglutide versus insulin glargine in participants with diabetes and CKD: AWARD-7 exploratory analysis. Kidney360 2021;2(2):254-62. [DOI: 10.34067/KID.0005852020] [PMID: 35373017] Tuttle KR, Rayner B, Lakshmanan MC, Woodward DB, Kwan A, Konig M, et al. Chronic kidney disease (CKD) outcomes with dulaglutide (DU) versus insulin glargine (IG) in type 2 diabetes and moderate-to-severe CKD by albuminuria status: AWARD-7 [abstract no: PS 082]. Diabetologia 2019;62(Suppl 1):S483-4.\n[DOI: 10.1007/s00125-019-4946-6] [EMBASE: 640482593]\nAWARD-PEDS 2022 {published data only}\n*  Arslanian SA, Hannon T, Zeitler P, Chao LC, Boucher-Berry C,\nBarrientos-Perez M, et al. Once-weekly dulaglutide for the\ntreatment of youths with type 2 diabetes. New England Journal\nof Medicine 2022;387(5):433-43. [DOI: 10.1056/NEJMoa2204601]\n[PMID: 35658022]\nBjornstad P, Arslanian S, Hannon T, Zeitler P, Francis J,\nCurtis A, et al. Dulaglutide and glomerular hyperfiltration\nand albuminuria in youth with type 2 diabetes: results from\nthe AWARD-PEDS study [abstract no: 709]. Diabetologia\n2023;66(Suppl 1):S360-1. [DOI: 10.1007/s00125-023-05969-6]\n[EMBASE: 642618867]\nBjornstad P, Arslanian SA, Hannon TS, Zeitler PS, Francis JL,\nCurtis AM, et al. Dulaglutide and glomerular hyperfiltration,\nproteinuria, and albuminuria in youth with type 2 diabetes:\npost hoc analysis of the AWARD-PEDS study. Diabetes Care\n2024;47(9):1617-21. [DOI: 10.2337/dc24-0322] [PMID: 38954432]\nDekkers 2021 {published data only}\n*  Dekkers IA, Bizino MB, Paiman EH, Smit JW, Jazet IM,\nde Vries AP, et al. The efect of glycemic control on renal\ntriglyceride content assessed by proton spectroscopy in\npatients with type 2 diabetes mellitus: a single-center parallel-\ngroup trial. Journal of Renal Nutrition 2021;31(6):611-9. [PMID:\n33293204]\nDUAL I 2014 {published data only}\nDi Bartolo P, Davidson J, Aroda V, Bode B, Rodbard H,\nAndersen A, et al. Insulin degludec/liraglutide is eficacious\nand safe in patients with type 2 diabetes with normal, mild\nor moderate renal impairment: Analyses from phase 3 trials\nGlucagon-like peptide 1 (GLP-1) receptor agonists for people with chronic kidney disease and diabetes (Review)\nCopyright © 2025 The Cochrane Collaboration. Published by John Wiley & Sons, Ltd.\n22\n",
