    "text": " \n \nNot pitting when chronic\n \n \nFavours lipoedema\n \n \nNot pitting\n \n \nSpares foot\n \n \nObese woman\n \nPND = paroxysmal nocturnal dyspnoea.\n \nSVT = supraventricular tachycardia.\n \nVT = ventricular tachycardia.\n \nAF = atrial fibrillation.\n \n* McGee S, Evidence-based clinical diagnosis, 2nd edn. St Louis: Saunders, 2007.\n† Khan NA, Rahim SA, Avand SS et al. Does the clinical examination predict lower extremity peripheral arterial\ndisease? JAMA 2006 Feb 1; 295(5):536–546.\nTable 4.7 Differential diagnosis of syncope and dizziness\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n",
