    "text": "Figure 4.3 Normal pressures (mmHg) and saturations (%) in the heart\n \nThe cardiac valves separate the atria from the ventricles (the\natrioventricular or mitral and tricuspid valves) and the ventricles from their\ncorresponding great vessels. Figure 4.4 shows the fibrous skeleton that\nsupports the four valves and their appearance during systole (cardiac\ncontraction) and diastole (cardiac relaxation).\nFigure 4.4 The cardiac valves in systole (a) and diastole (b)\n",
