    "text": " \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nSign\nPositive\nLR\nNegative\nLR\nDelayed carotid upstroke\n3.7\n0.4\nDiminished carotid pulse on palpation\n2.3\n0.3\nApical impulse sustained (pressure-\nloaded)\n4.1\n0.3\nAbsent or decreased A2\n3.6\n0.4\nS4 gallop\nNS\nNS\nLate peaking murmur\n4.4\n0.2\nLong murmur\n3.9\n0.2\nMurmur radiates to the neck\n1.4\n0.1\n \nNS = not significant.\n \nFrom McGee S, Evidence-based physical diagnosis, 2nd edn. St Louis: Saunders, 2007.\nAortic sclerosis presents in the elderly; there are none of the peripheral\n",
