  {
    "text": "Figure 6.6 Acanthosis nigricans: (a) axilla; (b) chest wall\nFrom McDonald FS, ed., Mayo Clinic images in internal medicine, with permission. © Mayo Clinic Scientific Press\nand CRC Press.\n \nFigure 6.7 (right) Hereditary haemorrhagic telangiectasia involving the lips\nFrom McDonald FS, ed., Mayo Clinic images in internal medicine, with permission. © Mayo Clinic Scientific Press\nand CRC Press.\n \nFigure 6.8 Porphyria cutanea tarda—scarring from photosensitivity\n \nTABLE 6.4 The skin and the gut\n \n",
