      "edition": ""
    }
  },
  {
    "text": " \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nColour\nUnderlying causes\nVery pale or\ncolourless\nDilute urine (e.g. overhydration, recent excessive\nbeer consumption, diabetes insipidus, post-\nobstructive diuresis)\nYellow-\norange\nConcentrated urine (e.g. dehydration)\nBilirubin\nTetracycline, anthracene, sulfasalazine, riboflavin,\nrifampin\nBrown\nBilirubin\nNitrofurantoin, phenothiazines; chloroquine, senna,\nrhubarb (yellow to brown or red)\nPink\nBeetroot consumption\nPhenindione, phenolphthalein (laxatives), uric acid\ncrystalluria (massive)\nRed\nHaematuria, haemoglobinuria, myoglobinuria (may\nalso be pink, brown or black)\nPorphyrins, rifampicin, phenazopyridine, phenytoin,\nbeetroot\nGreen\nMethylene blue, triamterene\nBlack\nSevere haemoglobinuria\nMethyldopa, metronidazole, unipenem\nMelanoma, ochronosis; porphryins, alkaptonuria (red\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "Clinical Examination-Talley & Connor-pdf.pdf",
      "page": 497,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "char_count": 817,
      "word_count": 85,
      "title": "Talley & Connor's Clinical Examination",
      "author": "Talley & Connor",
      "year": "2020",
