    }
  },
  {
    "text": "Figure 11.98 Sensory loss with transverse section of the spinal cord\n \nFigure 11.99 Pattern of sensory loss with intrinsic spinal cord disease\nFor example, central tumour or less commonly with extrinsic compression of the spinal cord\n—sacrum is spared.\n \n",
