    }
  },
  {
    "text": " \nWhen cognitive dysfunction is suspected, as in patients with dementia,5\na more detailed examination of cognitive function should be carried out. A\nwidely used tool for doing this is the mini-mental state examination,6 which\nassesses aspects of orientation, memory and concentration. Details of this\nexamination are shown in Table 12.7. Some of the common causes of\ndelirium and dementia are listed in Tables 12.8 and 12.9.\nTABLE 12.7 The mini-mental state examination\n \n",
