    "text": "patient is asked to stop breathing. Listen for a bruit that may be a sign of an\narteriovenous malformation or a vascular tumour.\n10. Feel for the pre-auricular node (adenoviral conjunctivitis).\nThe causes of common eye abnormalities are summarised in Table\n13.3.\nTABLE 13.3 Causes of eye abnormalities\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nCataracts\n1. Old age (senile cataract)\n2. Endocrine—e.g. diabetes mellitus, steroids\n3. Hereditary or congenital—e.g. dystrophia\nmyotonica, Refsum’s disease*\n4. Ocular disease—e.g. glaucoma\n5. Radiation\n6. Trauma\n \nPapilloedema vs papillitis\nPapilloedema\nPapillitis\nOptic disc swollen\nAcuity poor\n",
