      "edition": ""
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "107 \nCandidate Information and Tasks \n573 \nCondition 107 \nDandruff or head lice in a 6-year-old girl? \n \nCANDIDATE INFORMATION AND TASKS \nYou have just examined 6-year-old Jodie, who has been brought to a general practice by her mother because of an \nitchy scalp and what appears to be dandruff in her hair. \nHer parent is concerned that she may have lice in her hair which have been reported among other children at her \nschool. Jodie has excellent health otherwise. She has a 4-year-old brother who occasionally scratches his scalp. On \ninspection of her scalp you have found 'white specks' which are firmly stuck to the hairs as illustrated \nEyelashes and eyebrows show no abnormality. There is no scalp dermatitis, though some redness consistent with \nscratching is evident. \n \nYOUR TASK IS TO: \n• Explain your diagnosis and management plan to the parent, who is concerned as to whether this is lice or dandruff. \nCONDITION 107. FIGURE 1. \nThe Performance Guidelines for Condition 107 can be found on page 585\n",
