    "text": "114 \nCandidate Information and Tasks \n604 \nCondition 1 1 4  \nA lethargic febrile 2-year-old boy with a rash \n \nCANDIDATE INFORMATION AND TASKS \nA two-year-old boy is brought by his very upset parents to a general practice in a small country \ntown, 50 km from a regional city. The child has become lethargic and febrile in the last four hours. \nHe has had a mild upper respiratory tract infection for the last three days. Now he has a high \nfever, is uninterested in food, irritable and has very cold skin. He is an only child of healthy \nparents. \nOn examination, he looks unwell and has a fine nonspecific macular petechial rash on the trunk \nand legs as illustrated below. Elsewhere the skin is cold and pale, especially over the extremities. \nVital signs: \nTemperature \n40 \"C (tympanic measurement) \nRespiratory rate \n48/min \nPulse \n150/min \nBlood pressure \n90/60 mmHg \nNeck stiffness \nNone apparent \nYOUR TASKS ARE TO: \n• Explain the diagnostic possibilities to the parent. \n• Outline your management plan. \nCONDITION 114. FIGURE 1. \nThe Performance Guidelines for Condition 114 can be found on page 612\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "AMC Handbook of Clinical Assessment.pdf",
