    "text": "CONTENTS\b\nPage\nIntroduction\b\n2\nReferring Women to KEMH\t\n2\nReferral pathways\t\n5\nAntenatal shared care visits\b\n7\nPreconception counselling, folate and iodine\b\n8\nObstetric medication information\b\n9\nDocumentation and routine assessments\b\n9\nNon-medicare eligible patients\b\n10\nEarly Pregnancy Assessment Service (EPAS)\b\n10\nEmergency Centre\t\n11\nGuidelines for exclusion from shared care\b\n12\nPreterm birth (WA Preterm Birth Prevention Initiative)\b\n13\nGuidelines for immediate antenatal assessment\b\n14\nInfectious diseases and immunisation in pregnancy\t\n14\nInvestigations\b\n15\nVitamin Supplementation in pregnancy\b\n18\nObesity in pregnancy\b\n20\nGestational Diabetes Mellitus (GDM) screening\b\n22\nFetal anomaly screening\b\n26\nFetal morphology ultrasound \b\n30\nRural patients\b\n30\nMaternal Fetal Medicine Service (MFM)\t\n31\nMaternal Fetal Assessment Unit (MFAU)\t\n31\nWomen and newborn drug and alcohol service (WANDAS)\t\n31\nGuidelines for investigation of patients at risk of haemoglobinopathy\t\n32\nUse of anti-D in pregnancy\t\n35\nHow to obtain anti-D\b\n35\nPerinatal Mental Health Services\b\n37\nPostnatal complications\t\n39\nAppendix 1 – Edinburgh Postnatal Depression Scale (EPDS)\b\n42\nAppendix 2 – Perinatal Anxiety Screening Scale (PASS)\b\n44\nAppendix 3 – Care choices provided at KEMH\b\n46\nAppendix 4 – Important telephone numbers\b\n51\n",
