    "text": "46\nAppendix 3 – Care choices provided at KEMH\n1. FAMILY BIRTH CENTRE (FBC) / MIDWIFERY GROUP PRACTICE (MGP)\nDescription\nHealthy low risk women may self-refer or be referred by their GP. \nWomen are allocated to a primary midwife for their pregnancy, birth and \npostnatal care.   \nIf the primary midwife is unavailable, care will be provided by another midwife \nwithin the Midwifery Group Practice whom the woman will have met previously.\nIf the woman needs to be transferred to the main hospital, the MGP midwife will \nstay with the woman and provide care in collaboration with other health care \nprofessionals as appropriate.\nExclusion criteria include: women who have had a previous caesarean section \nor women with a BMI ≥ 30 at the time of booking.\nFor more information about the FBC, including exclusion criteria - click here\nPregnancy care\nFamily Birth Centre MGP midwife\nAntenatal and postnatal visits may occur within \nthe home.\nPlanned place of birth\nFamily Birth Centre (on-site at KEMH, access \nlocated off Railway Parade)\nCare provider during \nlabour and birth\nFamily Birth Centre MGP midwife.\nCare provider following \nthe birth\nFamily Birth Centre MGP midwife.\nPossible referrals of care\nTo Antenatal Clinic (ANC) for pregnancy \ncomplications.\nTo Labour and Birth Suite (L&BS) for birth \ncomplications.\nTo postnatal wards for complications such as \ninfection, bleeding, feeding problems.\nTransfer home \n4 to 6 hours following birth if no complications.\nMidwifery care at home\nFamily Birth Centre MGP midwife until day 5\nContact number\nFamily Birth Centre (08) 6458 1800.  \nWomen will be given the mobile number of their \nprimary midwife.\n",
