  },
  {
    "text": "50\nAppendix 3 – Care choices provided at KEMH (cont.)\n5. Community Midwifery Program (CMP)\nDescription\nMidwifery care provided for healthy women with uncomplicated pregnancies. \nClients suitable for CMP care must meet the inclusion criteria – click here\nPregnancy care\nWomen are allocated a primary and support \nmidwife who will provide continuity of care \nthroughout pregnancy, birth and the postnatal \nperiod.\nAppointments occur at home and in clinics\nCMP currently run clinics at the following places; \nKEMH, Cockburn, Rockingham, Joondalup and \nKalamunda.\nReferral to an obstetrician and/or GP during \npregnancy may be required.\nPlanned place of birth\nHome (water birth may be an option)\nBirth centre (FBC or Kalamunda)\nHospital (KEMH, Fiona Stanley, Armadale, \nRockingham)\nCare provider during \nlabour and birth\nPrimary or support midwife.\nCare provider following \nthe birth\nPrimary and support midwife.\nPossible referrals of care\nTo hospital for pregnancy, labour or postnatal \ncomplications\nTransfer home \nVariable depending on place of birth and any \ncomplications.\nMidwifery care at home\nPrimary and support midwife will visit regularly \nfor 2-4 weeks postnatally dependent on each \nwoman’s individual needs\nContact number\n(08) 9301 9227\n",
