    "text": "Patient-Related Problems: The Common Calls\n196\ntachycardia can occur during narcotic reversal and may \nresult in congestive heart failure in a patient with poor left \nventricular function.\nAntipyretics\nAntipyretics should not be prescribed for an adult patient with \nfever unless the cause of the fever is known or the fever itself \nis causing symptoms. (Refer to Chapter 12 for the approach \nto the febrile patient. See Table 17–4 for the dosages and side \neffects of acetaminophen and aspirin.)\n",
