  {
    "text": "Patient-Related Problems: The Common Calls\n234\nMajor threats to life \n• Obstruction of the upper airway\n• Tension pneumothorax\n• Cardiac tamponade\n• Air embolus\nObstruction of the upper airway may result from a massive soft \ntissue hematoma (e.g., caused by inadvertent puncture of the \nFigure 20–3  Causes of shortness of breath after central line \ninsertion. A, Pneumothorax. B, Massive soft tissue hematoma \nfrom inadvertent carotid artery puncture, resulting in obstruc-\ntion of the upper airway. C, Cardiac tamponade. D, Air embolus. \nE, Pleural effusion.\n",
