    "text": "474\nRATE\nMultiply the number of QRS complexes in a 6-second period \n(30 large squares) by 10 to obtain the number of beats per \nminute (Fig. C–1).\n• Normal: rate = 60 to 100 beats/min\n• Tachycardia: rate >100 beats/min\n• Bradycardia: rate <60 beats/min\nReading \nElectrocardiograms\nC\nFirst\ncomplex\nSecond\ncomplex\n300 150\n100\n75\n60\n3 sec\n0.5 mV\n0.04\nsec\n0.20 sec\nFigure C–1  Rate.\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "On Call Principles and Protocols.pdf",
      "page": 499,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
