    "text": "xviii\t\nContents\nCHAPTER 45\nApproaching infectious diseases\t\n834\nPyrexia of unknown origin\t\n834\nHistory\t\n835\nExamination\t\n835\nClinical scenarios for unexplained fever\t\n836\nHIV infection and AIDS\t\n836\nHistory\t\n837\nExamination\t\n838\nT&O’C essentials\t\n840\nOSCE revision topics – infectious  \ndiseases\t\n841\nReferences\t\n841\nSECTION 13\nMENTAL HEALTH HISTORY AND  \nEXAMINATION\t\n843\nCHAPTER 46\nThe psychiatric history and mental  \nstate examination\t\n845\nThe history\t\n845\nObtaining the history\t\n846\nIntroductory questions\t\n846\nHistory of the presenting illness\t\n846\nPast history and treatment history\t\n851\nFamily history\t\n853\nSocial and personal history\t\n853\nPremorbid personality\t\n854\nThe mental state examination\t\n854\nThe diagnosis\t\n854\nExamples of important psychiatric illnesses\t\n859\nDisorders that lead to physical illness\t\n859\nSchizophrenia\t\n860\nDepression\t\n861\nAnxiety disorders\t\n862\nPost-traumatic stress disorder (PTSD)\t\n862\nObsessive–compulsive disorder (OCD)\t\n863\nT&O’C essentials\t\n863\nOSCE revision topics – the psychiatric  \nhistory and the mental state examination\t\n863\nReferences\t\n863\nSECTION 14\nACUTE CARE AND END OF LIFE\t\n865\nCHAPTER 47\nThe acutely ill patient\t\n867\nInitial assessment\t\n867\nLevel of consciousness\t\n867\nDelirium\t\n867\nFurther examination\t\n868\nOSCE example – emergency care\t\n872\nReferences\t\n872\nCHAPTER 48\nThe pre-anaesthetic medical  \nevaluation (PAME)\t\n873\nThe history\t\n873\nCardiovascular history\t\n873\nThe respiratory history\t\n874\nOther\t\n874\nThe examination\t\n874\nCHAPTER 49\nAssessment of death\t\n875\nAssessment\t\n875\nDo-not-resuscitate (DNR) orders\t\n875\nDo not misdiagnose death\t\n875\nExamining a suspected death\t\n875\nInforming relatives\t\n876\nCompleting the death certificate\t\n876\nPostmortem\t\n877\nOrgan donation\t\n877\nSECTION 15\nADULT HISTORY TAKING AND  \nEXAMINATION IN THE WARDS  \nAND CLINICS\t\n879\nCHAPTER 50\nWriting and presenting the adult  \nhistory and physical examination\t\n881\nHistory\t\n881\nPhysical examination (PE)\t\n882\nProvisional diagnosis\t\n882\nProblem list and plans\t\n882\nContinuation notes\t\n882\nPresentation\t\n882\nReference\t\n885\nCHAPTER 51\nA suggested method for a rapid  \nscreening adult physical examination\t\n886\nHands and arms\t\n886\nFace\t\n886\nFront of the neck\t\n886\nChest\t\n886\nBack of the chest and neck\t\n886\nAbdomen\t\n887\nLegs\t\n887\nNeurological examination\t\n887\nCompleting the examination\t\n888\nIndex\t\nI-1\n",
