    "text": "CHAPTER 5  The cardiac examination\t\n101\nPDA\nb\nAR\nMS\nPR\n2\n3\n4\n5\nS3\nI\na\nAS\nVSD\nHCM\nMR\nPS\n2\n3\n4\n5\n\t(a)  Systolic murmurs:\nAS = aortic stenosis\nMR = mitral regurgitation\nHCM = hypertrophic cardiomyopathy\nPS = pulmonary stenosis\nVSD = ventricular septal defect\nI = innocent.\n\t(b)\t Diastolic murmurs and sounds:\nAR = aortic regurgitation\nMS = mitral stenosis\nS3 = third heart sound\nPR = pulmonary regurgitation\nPDA = patent ductus arteriosus (continuous murmur). \nFIGURE 5.35 \nSites of maximum intensity and radiation of murmurs and heart sounds \n(2–5 refer to intercostal spaces). \n",
