    "text": "\t\nCHAPTER 10  The respiratory examination\t\n185\nb\na\n(a) Percussing (plexor) finger poised; inset: plexor finger strikes pleximeter finger; (b) direct \npercussion of the clavicle for upper lobe resonance\nFIGURE 10.10 \nPercussion of the chest. \n2\n1\n4\n3\n6\n5\n8\n7\n10\n9\nApex\nNormal bronchial\nbreathing\nBronchial\nbreath sounds\nEnd of inspiration\nNormal\nbreath sounds\nAuscultate in each area shown (the numbers represent a suggested order). Distinguish normal \nbreath sounds from bronchial breathing\nFIGURE 10.11 \nNormal and bronchial breath sounds. \n",
