    "text": "\t\nCHAPTER 19  A SUMMARY OF THE EXAMINATION OF CHRONIC KIDNEYDISEASE\t\n325\nb\na\nUltrasound of (a) normal kidneys and \n(b) hydronephrosis with cortical atrophy \n(From Adam A, Dixon A, Gillard J et al. Grainger & Allison’s diagnostic \nradiology, 5th edn. Edinburgh: Churchill Livingstone, 2008.)\nFIGURE 19.4 \nUltrasound of polycystic kidneys. There are \nmultiple discrete cysts, the largest being \n1.2 × 1.2 centimetres \n(From Kaplan BS, Meyers K. Paediatric nephrology and urology: \nrequisites, 1st edn. St Louis, MO: Mosby, 2004.)\nFIGURE 19.5 \nNuclear scan of small scarred left kidney in a \npatient with hypertension. There is an area of \ninfarction in the upper pole of the right kidney \n(From Mason J, Pusey C. The kidney in systemic autoimmune diseases. \nVolume 7, Handbook of systemic autoimmune diseases. London: \nElsevier, 2007.)\nFIGURE 19.6 \nImaging the kidneys and scrotum\nSome common scan findings are presented in Figs \n19.4–19.8.\n",
