    "text": "352\t\nSECTION 6  The haematological system\nFilm shows a dysplastic \nnucleated RBC, frequent \nteardrop poikilocytes and a \nprimitive granulocyte \nFIGURE 22.8 \nMyelofibrosis. \nFilm shows two atypical or \n‘switched-on’ lymphocytes \nViral illness (e.g. infectious \nmononucleosis). \nFIGURE 22.10 \nThe two RBCs in the centre \nshow the trophozoite \nMalaria. \nFIGURE 22.9 \nThe WBC in the centre is a \nband form with prominent \n‘toxic’ granules \nFIGURE 22.11 \nBacterial infection (e.g. \npneumonia, infective \nendocarditis). \nThe film shows two very \nprimitive WBCs with \nprominent nucleoli \nFIGURE 22.12 \nAcute leukaemia. \nRBCs show varying shape \nand size; they are generally \nhypochromic \nIron-deficiency anaemia. \nFIGURE 22.13 \n",
