    "text": "CHAPTER 32  The neurological examination: general signs and the cranial nerves \t\n519\nf\ne\nd\nc\nb\na\n(a) Ahead, right eye down and out, ptosis. (b) Left failure of adduction (medial rectus). (c) \nRight abduction intact (lateral rectus [VI]). (d) Right up (failure of superior rectus [III]). (e) Left \nup (failure of interior oblique [III]). (f) Right down (failure of inferior rectus [III]) \nFIGURE 32.18 \nThird nerve palsy. \n",
