    "text": "526\t\nSECTION 9  The nervous system\n\t\nFrontalis muscle\nOrbicularis oculi\nOrbicularis oris\nBuccinator muscle\nChorda \ntympani nerve\nTaste to anterior\n2/3 of tongue\nStapedius muscle\nTympanic plexus\nStylomastoid \nforamen\nSuperior \nsalivatory\nnucleus\nMotor nucleus of VII\nNucleus of \ntractus\nsolitarius\nNote: The branches of the facial nerve: ‘Two zebras bit my car’—temporal, zygotic, buccal, \nmandibular, cervical \nFIGURE 32.28 \nThe facial nerve (cranial nerve VII). \nLeft upper motor neurone facial weakness, \nshowing drooping of the corner of the \nmouth, flattened nasolabial fold and sparing \nof the forehead; the lesion is in the right side \nof the brain \nFIGURE 32.29 \nCranial nerve VII: ‘Look up to wrinkle your \nforehead’ (normal) \nFIGURE 32.30 \n",
