    "text": "\t\nCHAPTER 36  A SUMMARY OF THE NEUROLOGICAL EXAMINATION\t\n613\nb\na\nThis is the typical appearance of a brain tumour on MRI, in this case a cerebellar \nmedulloblastoma. (a) The tumour has a low signal on spin-echo T1-weighted images. (b) After \ninjection of gadolinium (a contrast agent) the tumour enhances avidly, indicating a \nbreakdown of the blood–brain barrier \n(From Adam A. Grainger & Allison’s diagnostic radiology, 5th edn. Edinburgh: Churchill Livingstone, 2008.)\nFIGURE 36.6 \nCerebellar tumour. \n",
