    "text": "798\t\nSECTION 12  SPECIALTY SYSTEM HISTORY AND EXAMINATION\nOSCE REVISION TOPICS – EYES, EARS, NOSE \nAND THROAT\nUse these topics, which commonly occur in the OSCE, to \nhelp with revision.\n1.\t This woman has experienced some loss of vision. \nPlease take a history and then examine her. (pp 772, \n797)\n2.\t This woman complains of painful red eyes. Please \nexamine her. (pp 772, 797)\n3.\t This man has double vision. Please examine him.  \n(p 506)\n4.\t This man with diabetes mellitus has problems with \nhis vision. Please examine his fundi. His pupils have \nbeen dilated. (pp 776, 797)\n5.\t This woman has a sore throat. Please examine her. \n(pp 792, 798)\n6.\t This woman reports that she has sinusitis again. \nPlease examine her. (p 790)\n7.\t This man has mouth ulcers. Please take a history \nand then examine him. (p 792)\n8.\t This man has noticed a problem with deafness. Please \ntake a history and then examine him (speak loudly). \n(p 783)\nReferences\n1.\t Robinett DA, Kahn DH. The physical examination of the eye. Emerg Med Clin \nNorth Am 2008; 26:1–16. An excellent summary of eye anatomy and \nexamination.\n2.\t McGee S. Evidence-based clinical diagnosis, 3rd edn. St Louis: Saunders, 2012.\n3.\t Bagai A, Thavendiranathan P, Detsky AS. Does this patient have hearing \nimpairment? JAMA 2006; 295(4):416–428.\n4.\t Gwaltney JM, Sydnor A, Sande MA. Etiology and antimicrobial treatment of \nacute sinusitis. Ann Otol Rhinol Larygol Suppl 1981; 90(3 pt 3):68–71.\n5.\t Ebell MH, Call M, Shinholser J, Gardner J. The Rational Clinical Examination \nSystematic Review. Does this patient have infectious mononucleosis? JAMA \n2016; 315(14):1502–1509.\n6.\t McIsaac WJ, Kellner JD, Aufricht P et al. Empirical validation of guidelines for \nthe management of pharyngitis in children and adults. JAMA 2004; \n291(13):1587–1595.\n7.\t Cirilli AR. Emergency evaluation and management of the sore throat. Emerg \nMed Clin North Am 2013; 31(2):501–515.\nOSCE EXAMPLES  continued\n7.\t Test hearing, and perform Weber’s and Rinné’s tests.\n8.\t Palpate the temporomandibular joint for tenderness \nand crepitus (referred pain).\n9.\t Examine the throat for inflammation (referred pain).\nE. THROAT EXAMINATION\nMs Peta Smith complains of recurrent sore throat. Please \nexamine her.\n1.\t Put on gloves and remove any dentures. Note any \ndrooling or flushing or whether the patient appears \nill.\n2.\t Take a torch and ask the patient to open wide.\n3.\t Inspect the mouth and pharynx using a tongue \ndepressor. Note tonsillar enlargement and any ery-\nthema or other signs of inflammation.\n4.\t Note whether the patient cannot open the mouth \nfully (trismus).\n5.\t Feel the oral cavity and tongue gently with a gloved \nfinger.\n",
