    "text": "\t\nCHAPTER 43  The skin and lumps\t\n803\nSites of some important skin lesions of the limbs, face and trunk. \nThe dermatological examination: a suggested method continued\nOedema\nInjection marks\nScalp alopecia\nSeborrhoeic dermatitis\nPsoriasis\nSolar keratoses\nAcanthosis nigricans\nAcne rosacea\nSLE\nMalar flush\nNails:\n• Paronychia\n• Psoriasis\n• Clubbing\n• Splinter haemorrhages\nHands:\n• Scabies \n• Warts\n• Photosensitivity\n• Raynaud’s phenomenon\n• Scleroderma\nNits\nSebaceous cysts\nMetastases\nSeborrhoeic dermatitis\nDermatomyositis\nXanthelasma\nHerpes simplex\nCyanosis\nSpider naevi, gynaecomastia\nScratch marks\nArms:\nExtensor surface:\n• Psoriasis\n• Dermatitis \nherpetiformis\nFlexor surface:\n• Lichen planus\nGroin:\n• Warts\n• Herpes\n• Chancre\n• Discharge\n• Scrotal scabies\nShins:\n• Erythema nodosum\n• Erythema multiforme\n• Pyoderma\nUlcers\nFeet:\n• Trophic ulcers\n• Ischaemia\nKeratoderma\nSLE = systemic lupus erythematosus\nFIGURE 43.5 \nTEXT BOX 43.1 \nContinued\n",
