    "text": "A\na wave, 90–91\nabdomen\nacute\nafter blunt trauma, 274\ndifferential diagnosis of, 273f\nexamination of, 272–274, 273b, 281b\nauscultation of, 260–261, 260f, 312\nbloating of, 225–226\nin cardiac examination, 106\nchronic constrictive pericarditis and, 123\nCT of, 289–290, 291f, 293t\ndiabetes mellitus and, 469\ndistension of, 245–246, 245f\nexamination of, paediatric, 674t\nin gastrointestinal examination, 244–261\nin genitourinary examination, 310–312\nin gynaecological examination, 752\nin haematological examination, 343\ninspection of, 244–248\nintra-abdominal masses of, 249b\nmasses in, 248f, 253–257, 255b\npain in, 217–218\npalpation of, 248–257, 310, 311b\npercussion of, 257–258, 311–312\nin pregnancy, 737–738, 738f, 740f\nregions of, 249f\nin respiratory examination, 188\nRVF and, 120\nsample questions for, 621b\nscars of, 245, 245f\nshort stature and, 474\nskin lesions on, 247\nstriae of, 460f\nultrasound of, 287–289\ndensities in, 289t\nterminology for, 289t\nveins in, 246, 246f\nX-ray of, 285–287, 286t\nabdominal reflex, 575f\nabdominal wall, 256–257, 257b\nabdominojugular reflux test, 91\nabducens nerve, 503t, 510–521\npaediatric examination of, 653\npalsy, 518\nadrenals, 458–461\ntumour, 484f\nadrenocorticotrophic hormone (ACTH), 454\nadvance care planning, in history taking, 33\nadvance directive, 875\nadvance health directives, 33\nadverse reactions, 13\naffect, 852t\naffective disorders, 847t–850t\nage-appropriate visual acuity charts, 654f\nagitation, 852t\nagoraphobia, 847t–850t\nagraphaesthesia, 544f, 545\nagraphia, 543\nAIDS see acquired immunodeficiency \nsyndrome\nairway, unconscious patients and, 601–602\nairways disease, 166–168\nalanine transaminase (ALT), 285\nalcohol use, 17–18, 18b\nin HEADSSS assessment, 620t\nallergy, to drugs, 13\nalleviating factors, 8\nalopecia, 414\namaurosis fugax, 505\nambiguous genitalia, in neonatal \nexamination, 717\namblyopia, 507\namenorrhoea, 729–730, 745–747, 748b, 860\namiodarone facies, 42f\nAMPLE mnemonic, 867\nanaemia, 307, 350–354\ncauses of, 353b\niron-deficiency, 352f\nmegaloblastic, 354f\npallor and, 44–45\npalms and, 236\npernicious, 340\nin physical examination, 44–45\nquestions for patient with, 331b\nsickle cell, 351f\nspherocytic, 351f\nanal examination, paediatric, 678\nanal fissure, 265\nanalgesics, 18–19\nPage numbers followed by “f ” indicate figures, “t” indicate tables, and “b” indicate boxes.\nIndex\nABI see ankle-brachial index\nabnormal limb movements, in neonatal \nexamination, 699–700\nabscesses\nbrain, 614f\nsubmandibular, 795f\nabuse, elder, 33\nacalculia, 543\nacanthosis nigricans, 231–232, 232f\naccessory nerve, 503t, 532f, 533–534, \n534f\npalsy, 534\naccommodation, 512\nAchilles tendon, xanthomata in, 113\nachondroplasia, 47f, 473–475\nacid regurgitation, 219–220\nin pregnancy, 730\nacquired immunodeficiency syndrome \n(AIDS), 836\nacromegalic facies, 42f\nacromegaly, 456–458, 456f–457f\nACTH see adrenocorticotrophic hormone\naction plan, 14–15\nactive movement, 373–374\nactivities, in HEADSSS assessment, 620t\nactivities of daily living (ADL), 31–32, 826, \n828, 829b\nacute aortic dissection, 122\nacute arterial occlusion, 114\nacute cardiac tamponade, 123\nacute coronary syndrome, 62, 63t, 121\nacute inflammatory polyradiculoneuropathy, \n583–584\nacute otitis media (AOM), 647\nacute pericarditis, 122\nacute respiratory infection, 168\nacute stress disorder, 847t–850t\nacutely ill patient, assessment of, 867–872, \n869f\nAddison’s disease, 461, 461f, 483\nadduction, 386\nadenomyosis, 761t\nadenoviral conjunctivitis, 778\nadherence, of elderly patients, 32\nADL see activities of daily living\nadrenal insufficiency, causes of, 461b\n",
