      "year": "2020",
      "edition": ""
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "Normal Impulse Conduction\nSinoatrial node\nAV node\nBundle of His\nBundle Branches\nPurkinje fibers\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "ECG book.pdf",
      "page": 4,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "char_count": 96,
      "word_count": 14,
      "title": "Ecg Book",
      "author": "Unknown Author",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": ""
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "Impulse Conduction & the ECG\nSinoatrial node\nAV node\nBundle of His\nBundle Branches\nPurkinje fibers\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "ECG book.pdf",
      "page": 5,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "char_count": 99,
      "word_count": 16,
      "title": "Ecg Book",
      "author": "Unknown Author",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": ""
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "The “PQRST”\n• P wave - Atrial \ndepolarization\n• T wave - Ventricular \nrepolarization\n• QRS - Ventricular \ndepolarization\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "ECG book.pdf",
      "page": 6,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "char_count": 121,
      "word_count": 19,
      "title": "Ecg Book",
      "author": "Unknown Author",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": ""
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "The PR Interval\nAtrial depolarization \n+\ndelay in AV junction\n(AV node/Bundle of His)\n(delay allows time for \nthe atria to contract \nbefore the ventricles \ncontract)\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "ECG book.pdf",
      "page": 7,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "char_count": 166,
      "word_count": 26,
      "title": "Ecg Book",
      "author": "Unknown Author",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": ""
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "Pacemakers of the Heart\n• SA Node - Dominant pacemaker \n(60 - 100 beats/minute)\n• AV Node - Back-up pacemaker \n(40 - 60 beats/minute)\n• Ventricular cells - Back-up pacemaker \n(20 - 45 beats/minute)\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "ECG book.pdf",
      "page": 8,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "char_count": 198,
      "word_count": 34,
      "title": "Ecg Book",
      "author": "Unknown Author",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": ""
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "The ECG Paper\n• Horizontally\n– One small box - 0.04 s\n– One large box - 0.20 s \n• Vertically\n– One large box - 0.5 mV\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "ECG book.pdf",
      "page": 9,
      "chunk_index": 0,
      "total_chunks": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "char_count": 118,
      "word_count": 28,
      "title": "Ecg Book",
      "author": "Unknown Author",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": ""
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "The ECG Paper (cont)\n• Every 3 seconds (15 large boxes) is \nmarked by a vertical line.\n• This helps when calculating the heart \nrate.\n3 sec\n3 sec\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "ECG book.pdf",
      "page": 10,
      "type": "list",
      "char_count": 146,
      "word_count": 29,
      "title": "Ecg Book",
      "author": "Unknown Author",
      "year": "2020",
      "edition": ""
    }
  },
  {
    "text": "End of Module I\nECG Basics\n",
    "metadata": {
      "source": "ECG book.pdf",
